{"12870":[{"footnoteId":4095,"paragraphs":[{"pid":916,"text":"“Man.” Heb., ʼish."}]},{"footnoteId":4096,"paragraphs":[{"pid":917,"text":"“Job.” Heb., ʼI·yohvʹ, meaning “Object of Hostility.” Not the same as weYohvʹ, “and Iob,” in Ge 46:13."}]}],"12872":[{"footnoteId":4097,"paragraphs":[{"pid":918,"text":"Or, “small cattle,” including sheep and goats."}]},{"footnoteId":4098,"paragraphs":[{"pid":919,"text":"Lit., “sons of the East.”"}]}],"12873":[{"footnoteId":4099,"paragraphs":[{"pid":920,"text":"“Each one.” Heb., ʼish."}]}],"12874":[{"footnoteId":4100,"paragraphs":[{"pid":921,"text":"“Have cursed” was the original reading. The text was changed to read “have blessed.” LXX, “thought bad things against”; Sy, “reviled”; Vg, “blessed.” See App 2B."}]}],"12875":[{"footnoteId":4101,"paragraphs":[{"pid":922,"text":"“Sons of.” Heb., benehʹ; LXX, “angels.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4102,"paragraphs":[{"pid":923,"text":"“The [true] God.” Heb., ha·ʼElo·himʹ, the definite article ha, “the,” preceding the title ʼElo·himʹ. See App 1F."}]},{"footnoteId":4103,"paragraphs":[{"pid":924,"text":"Heb., has·Sa·tanʹ, “the Resister.” Used throughout chapters 1 and 2. This is the first occurrence of has·Sa·tanʹ in M, although sa·tanʹ, “resister,” without the definite article ha, occurs nine times before this, beginning in Nu 22:22. Gesenius’ Hebrew Grammar (GK), §126 d and e, states: “The article is, generally speaking, employed to determine a substantive wherever it is required by Greek and English; thus: . . . (d) When terms applying to whole classes are restricted (simply by usage) to particular individuals . . . or things, e.g. שָׂטָן adversary, הַשָּׂטָן the adversary, Satan . . . .”"}]}],"12880":[{"footnoteId":4104,"paragraphs":[{"pid":925,"text":"See vs 5 ftn."}]}],"12881":[{"footnoteId":4105,"paragraphs":[{"pid":926,"text":"Lit., “face.” See 2Sa 17:11 ftn, “Person.”"}]}],"12884":[{"footnoteId":4106,"paragraphs":[{"pid":927,"text":"Lit., “Sheba.”"}]}],"12888":[{"footnoteId":4107,"paragraphs":[{"pid":928,"text":"“Wind.” Heb., ruʹach. See Ge 1:2 ftn, “Force.”"}]}],"12892":[{"footnoteId":4108,"paragraphs":[{"pid":929,"text":"“The angels,” LXX."}]},{"footnoteId":4109,"paragraphs":[{"pid":930,"text":"See 1:6 ftn, “Satan.”"}]}],"12895":[{"footnoteId":4110,"paragraphs":[{"pid":931,"text":"“His soul (life).” Heb., naph·shohʹ; Gr., psy·khesʹ; Lat., aʹni·ma. See App 4A."}]}],"12896":[{"footnoteId":4111,"paragraphs":[{"pid":932,"text":"See 1:5 ftn."}]}],"12897":[{"footnoteId":4112,"paragraphs":[{"pid":933,"text":"See vs 4 ftn."}]}],"12898":[{"footnoteId":4113,"paragraphs":[{"pid":934,"text":"See 1:12 ftn."}]}],"12900":[{"footnoteId":4114,"paragraphs":[{"pid":935,"text":"See 1:5 ftn."}]}],"12907":[{"footnoteId":4115,"paragraphs":[{"pid":936,"text":"“An able-bodied man.” Heb., ghaʹver."}]}],"12908":[{"footnoteId":4116,"paragraphs":[{"pid":937,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah, sing. of ʼElo·himʹ. ʼElohʹah occurs 41 times in Job and 16 times in other books of M. See De 32:15 ftn, “God.”"}]}],"12909":[{"footnoteId":4117,"paragraphs":[{"pid":938,"text":"Lit., “death shadow.”"}]}],"12912":[{"footnoteId":4118,"paragraphs":[{"pid":939,"text":"“Cursers of.” Heb., ʼo·rerehʹ; not the same as in 1:5, 11; 2:5, 9."}]},{"footnoteId":4119,"paragraphs":[{"pid":940,"text":"“Leviathan,” MSyVg; LXX, “the great sea monster.”"}]}],"12918":[{"footnoteId":4120,"paragraphs":[{"pid":941,"text":"“Pyramids,” by a correction."}]}],"12923":[{"footnoteId":4121,"paragraphs":[{"pid":942,"text":"“From his master.” Heb., me·ʼadho·navʹ, pl. of ʼa·dhohnʹ, to denote excellence."}]}],"12926":[{"footnoteId":4122,"paragraphs":[{"pid":943,"text":"“At a stone heap,” by a slight correction of M, to correspond with “burial place” in the same vs."}]}],"12927":[{"footnoteId":4123,"paragraphs":[{"pid":944,"text":"“To able-bodied man.” Heb., legheʹver. See vs 3 ftn."}]},{"footnoteId":4124,"paragraphs":[{"pid":945,"text":"See vs 4 ftn."}]}],"12932":[{"footnoteId":4125,"paragraphs":[{"pid":946,"text":"“Word.” Heb., dha·varʹ, used 20 times in Job."}]}],"12934":[{"footnoteId":4126,"paragraphs":[{"pid":947,"text":"“Your words.” Heb., mil·leyʹkha, used 34 times in Job and only 4 times in other books."}]}],"12940":[{"footnoteId":4127,"paragraphs":[{"pid":948,"text":"Heb., ʼar·yehʹ. An African lion."}]}],"12941":[{"footnoteId":4128,"paragraphs":[{"pid":949,"text":"Heb., la·viʼʹ. An Asian lion."}]}],"12947":[{"footnoteId":4129,"paragraphs":[{"pid":950,"text":"“Mortal man.” Heb., ha·ʼenohshʹ."}]},{"footnoteId":4130,"paragraphs":[{"pid":951,"text":"“Than God.” Heb., me·ʼElohʹah."}]}],"12948":[{"footnoteId":4131,"paragraphs":[{"pid":952,"text":"Or, “angels.”"}]}],"12949":[{"footnoteId":4132,"paragraphs":[{"pid":953,"text":"Or, “They are crushed.”"}]}],"12952":[{"footnoteId":4133,"paragraphs":[{"pid":954,"text":"“Which one of the holy angels,” LXX."}]}],"12956":[{"footnoteId":4134,"paragraphs":[{"pid":955,"text":"Lit., “Which his harvest [is].”"}]},{"footnoteId":4135,"paragraphs":[{"pid":956,"text":"Or, “even out of the thorns.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4136,"paragraphs":[{"pid":957,"text":"“And thirsty ones do draw out their milk,” by a correction of M."}]}],"12958":[{"footnoteId":4137,"paragraphs":[{"pid":958,"text":"Or, “earthling man.” Heb., ʼa·dhamʹ."}]},{"footnoteId":4138,"paragraphs":[{"pid":959,"text":"Lit., “the sons of flame.”"}]}],"12959":[{"footnoteId":4139,"paragraphs":[{"pid":960,"text":"Or, “the Divine One.” Heb., ʼEl; LXX, “Jehovah.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4140,"paragraphs":[{"pid":961,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElo·himʹ, pl. of ʼElohʹah, to denote excellence and majesty; LXX, “Jehovah.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4141,"paragraphs":[{"pid":962,"text":"Or, “suit.”"}]}],"12960":[{"footnoteId":4142,"paragraphs":[{"pid":963,"text":"Lit., “and there is no searching [of them].”"}]}],"12968":[{"footnoteId":4143,"paragraphs":[{"pid":964,"text":"Or, “mortal man,” as in 4:17. Heb., ʼenohshʹ."}]},{"footnoteId":4144,"paragraphs":[{"pid":965,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah."}]}],"12971":[{"footnoteId":4145,"paragraphs":[{"pid":966,"text":"Lit., “hands.”"}]}],"12982":[{"footnoteId":4146,"paragraphs":[{"pid":967,"text":"“Jehovah,” LXXVg."}]},{"footnoteId":4147,"paragraphs":[{"pid":968,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah."}]},{"footnoteId":4148,"paragraphs":[{"pid":969,"text":"“Cast me out from social intercourse,” by the transposition of two letters in M."}]}],"12983":[{"footnoteId":4149,"paragraphs":[{"pid":970,"text":"Or, “onager; wild ass.”"}]}],"12986":[{"footnoteId":4150,"paragraphs":[{"pid":971,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah."}]}],"12989":[{"footnoteId":4151,"paragraphs":[{"pid":972,"text":"Or, “my life [as a soul].” Heb., naph·shiʹ; Gr., psy·kheʹ."}]}],"12992":[{"footnoteId":4152,"paragraphs":[{"pid":973,"text":"Or, “loyal love.”"}]}],"12997":[{"footnoteId":4153,"paragraphs":[{"pid":974,"text":"Lit., “Sheba.”"}]}],"13003":[{"footnoteId":4154,"paragraphs":[{"pid":975,"text":"“Reproving.” In Heb. this is a verb in the infinitive absolute, indefinite as to time and impersonal."}]}],"13019":[{"footnoteId":4155,"paragraphs":[{"pid":976,"text":"“My spirit.” Heb., ru·chiʹ; Lat., spiʹri·tus."}]}],"13025":[{"footnoteId":4156,"paragraphs":[{"pid":977,"text":"Or, “make much of him.”"}]}],"13027":[{"footnoteId":4157,"paragraphs":[{"pid":978,"text":"That is, alone for the briefest time. See Nu 4:20 ftn."}]}],"13028":[{"footnoteId":4158,"paragraphs":[{"pid":979,"text":"“Mankind.” Heb., ha·ʼa·dhamʹ."}]},{"footnoteId":4159,"paragraphs":[{"pid":980,"text":"“You,” LXX and the original Heb. text; M, “myself.” This is one of the Eighteen Emendations of the Jewish Sopherim. See App 2B."}]}],"13032":[{"footnoteId":4160,"paragraphs":[{"pid":981,"text":"“God.” Heb., ha·ʼElʹ. Here ha is an interrogative particle introducing a question."}]}],"13035":[{"footnoteId":4161,"paragraphs":[{"pid":982,"text":"According to M; LXX, “he will listen to your supplication.”"}]}],"13039":[{"footnoteId":4162,"paragraphs":[{"pid":983,"text":"“Tell you,” LXX; M, “say to you.”"}]}],"13042":[{"footnoteId":4163,"paragraphs":[{"pid":984,"text":"“Pathways,” M; LXX, “the final things (outcome); the end afterward.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4164,"paragraphs":[{"pid":985,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl; LXX, “Jehovah.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4165,"paragraphs":[{"pid":986,"text":"Or, “ungodly (profane) one”; or, “anyone alienated from God.”"}]}],"13043":[{"footnoteId":4166,"paragraphs":[{"pid":987,"text":"Or, “web.”"}]}],"13049":[{"footnoteId":4167,"paragraphs":[{"pid":988,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]}],"13053":[{"footnoteId":4168,"paragraphs":[{"pid":989,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl; LXX, “Jehovah.”"}]}],"13058":[{"footnoteId":4169,"paragraphs":[{"pid":990,"text":"“To the sun.” Heb., la·cheʹres; Gr., he·liʹoi; Lat., soʹli."}]}],"13059":[{"footnoteId":4170,"paragraphs":[{"pid":991,"text":"Lit., “high places.”"}]}],"13060":[{"footnoteId":4171,"paragraphs":[{"pid":992,"text":"“The Ash constellation.” Heb., ʽAsh. Thought by some to be the constellation Ursa Major (Great Bear)."}]},{"footnoteId":4172,"paragraphs":[{"pid":993,"text":"“The Kesil constellation.” Heb., Kesilʹ. Thought by some to be the constellation Orion."}]},{"footnoteId":4173,"paragraphs":[{"pid":994,"text":"“And the Kimah constellation.” Heb., weKhi·mahʹ. Thought by some to be the Pleiades stars in the Taurus constellation."}]},{"footnoteId":4174,"paragraphs":[{"pid":995,"text":"“The One making the Pleiades and Hesperus and Arcturus and the storerooms of the South,” LXX; Vg, “who makes Arcturus and Orion and the Hyades and the interior rooms of the South.” The interior rooms of the South are understood to be the constellations below the equator, in the southern hemisphere."}]}],"13064":[{"footnoteId":4175,"paragraphs":[{"pid":996,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah. See 3:4 ftn."}]},{"footnoteId":4176,"paragraphs":[{"pid":997,"text":"“Stormer.” Heb., raʹhav. See 26:12 ftn."}]}],"13069":[{"footnoteId":4177,"paragraphs":[{"pid":998,"text":"“Taking.” In Heb. this is a verb in the infinitive absolute, indefinite as to time and is here used as the object of the verb “grant.”"}]}],"13070":[{"footnoteId":4178,"paragraphs":[{"pid":999,"text":"“There he is,” T; M, “look!”"}]}],"13071":[{"footnoteId":4179,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1000,"text":"“My own mouth,” MLXXSyVg; by a correction of M, “his own mouth.”"}]}],"13074":[{"footnoteId":4180,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1001,"text":"“Scourge,” by another derivation of the Heb. word."}]}],"13081":[{"footnoteId":4181,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1002,"text":"Or, “palms.”"}]}],"13084":[{"footnoteId":4182,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1003,"text":"“There exists no,” MVg; LXX, “If only there were.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4183,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1004,"text":"Or, “mediator.” Gr., me·siʹtes, as in 1Ti 2:5."}]}],"13087":[{"footnoteId":4184,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1005,"text":"“About myself,” MVg; LXX, “about him.”"}]}],"13088":[{"footnoteId":4185,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1006,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah."}]}],"13089":[{"footnoteId":4186,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1007,"text":"Or, “palms.”"}]}],"13098":[{"footnoteId":4187,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1008,"text":"Or, “loyal love.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4188,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1009,"text":"“My spirit (breath).” Heb., ru·chiʹ; Gr., pneuʹma; Lat., spiʹri·tum."}]}],"13103":[{"footnoteId":4189,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1010,"text":"“Witnesses,” MVg; LXX, “testing”; Sy, “weapons.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4190,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1011,"text":"Or, “one shift of compulsory labor after another is with me.”"}]}],"13104":[{"footnoteId":4191,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1012,"text":"Or, “Let me expire.”"}]}],"13107":[{"footnoteId":4192,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1013,"text":"Lit., “death shadow.”"}]}],"13110":[{"footnoteId":4193,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1014,"text":"Lit., “a man of lips.”"}]}],"13111":[{"footnoteId":4194,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1015,"text":"“Men.” Heb., methimʹ, adult males."}]}],"13114":[{"footnoteId":4195,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1016,"text":"Lit., “doubled.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4196,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1017,"text":"Lit., “And know you,” imperative."}]}],"13119":[{"footnoteId":4197,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1018,"text":"See vs 3 ftn."}]}],"13120":[{"footnoteId":4198,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1019,"text":"“Even a . . . man.” Heb., weʼishʹ."}]},{"footnoteId":4199,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1020,"text":"Or, “an earthling man.” Heb., ʼa·dhamʹ."}]}],"13127":[{"footnoteId":4200,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1021,"text":"Lit., “soften your face.”"}]}],"13131":[{"footnoteId":4201,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1022,"text":"Lit., “I am not falling behind you.”"}]}],"13132":[{"footnoteId":4202,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1023,"text":"“I,” MVg; LXXSy, “he.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4203,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1024,"text":"“To God.” Heb., le·ʼElohʹah."}]}],"13134":[{"footnoteId":4204,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1025,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]},{"footnoteId":4205,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1026,"text":"“A god.” Heb., ʼelohʹah."}]}],"13136":[{"footnoteId":4206,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1027,"text":"Or, “Or speak thoughtfully to the earth.” By a correction, “Or the reptiles [or, wild beasts] of the earth.”"}]}],"13137":[{"footnoteId":4207,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1028,"text":"“Jehovah,” MLXXSyVg; T(Aram.), Yai."}]}],"13138":[{"footnoteId":4208,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1029,"text":"“And the spirit (breath) of.” Heb., weruʹach; Gr., pneuʹma; Syr., weru·chaʼ; Lat., spiʹri·tus."}]},{"footnoteId":4209,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1030,"text":"“Man.” Heb., ʼish."}]}],"13140":[{"footnoteId":4210,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1031,"text":"Or, “and does not length of days mean understanding?”"}]}],"13145":[{"footnoteId":4211,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1032,"text":"“The One leading counselors captive,” LXX; Vg, “he leads counselors on to a foolish end.”"}]}],"13146":[{"footnoteId":4212,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1033,"text":"By a change of vowel pointing. Lit., “discipline.”"}]}],"13147":[{"footnoteId":4213,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1034,"text":"Or, “and overflowing rivers he causes to run dry.”"}]}],"13148":[{"footnoteId":4214,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1035,"text":"Lit., “lip.”"}]}],"13155":[{"footnoteId":4215,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1036,"text":"See 12:3 ftn."}]}],"13156":[{"footnoteId":4216,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1037,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]}],"13163":[{"footnoteId":4217,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1038,"text":"“Show partiality,” M; TSyVg, “treat him with partiality.”"}]}],"13165":[{"footnoteId":4218,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1039,"text":"Or, “your breastworks.”"}]}],"13167":[{"footnoteId":4219,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1040,"text":"“And . . . my own soul.” Heb., wenaph·shiʹ; Gr., psy·khenʹ; Lat., aʹni·mam. Compare Jg 12:3; 1Sa 19:5."}]}],"13168":[{"footnoteId":4220,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1041,"text":"Or, “I would not wait,” M; MmarginTSyVg, “for him I would wait.”"}]}],"13169":[{"footnoteId":4221,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1042,"text":"Or, “That.”"}]}],"13173":[{"footnoteId":4222,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1043,"text":"“Do.” The Heb. verb is sing. to agree with “you” and “your(s)” addressed to God in vss 20-27."}]}],"13180":[{"footnoteId":4223,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1044,"text":"Lit., “roots of.”"}]}],"13181":[{"footnoteId":4224,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1045,"text":"“He,” that is, Job."}]},{"footnoteId":4225,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1046,"text":"“Something rotten (rottenness),” MVg; LXX, “skin bag”; Sy, “leather bag.”"}]}],"13182":[{"footnoteId":4226,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1047,"text":"Or, “Earthling man.” Heb., ʼa·dhamʹ."}]}],"13183":[{"footnoteId":4227,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1048,"text":"Lit., “keep standing.” See Ex 9:16 ftn, “Existence.”"}]}],"13184":[{"footnoteId":4228,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1049,"text":"“Me,” M; LXXSyVg, “him.”"}]}],"13185":[{"footnoteId":4229,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1050,"text":"Or, “No one can.”"}]}],"13187":[{"footnoteId":4230,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1051,"text":"Or, “may cease,” as in vs 7."}]}],"13188":[{"footnoteId":4231,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1052,"text":"Lit., “yet change.”"}]}],"13191":[{"footnoteId":4232,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1053,"text":"“But an able-bodied man.” Heb., wegheʹver."}]},{"footnoteId":4233,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1054,"text":"“An earthling man.” Heb., ʼa·dhamʹ."}]},{"footnoteId":4234,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1055,"text":"“Where is he?” MVg; LXXSy, “he is no more.”"}]}],"13193":[{"footnoteId":4235,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1056,"text":"Lit., “And man.” Heb., weʼishʹ."}]},{"footnoteId":4236,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1057,"text":"“He will not wake up, nor will he rouse himself from his sleep,” Vg and by a slight correction of M."}]}],"13194":[{"footnoteId":4237,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1058,"text":"“In Sheol.” Heb., bish·ʼohlʹ; Gr., haiʹdei; Syr., ba·shiul; Lat., in·ferʹno; that is, the common grave of mankind. See App 4B."}]}],"13195":[{"footnoteId":4238,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1059,"text":"“An able-bodied man.” Heb., geʹver."}]}],"13200":[{"footnoteId":4239,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1060,"text":"“Mortal man.” Heb., ʼenohshʹ."}]}],"13203":[{"footnoteId":4240,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1061,"text":"Or, “Only his own kin (fleshly relatives) will keep aching for him, and his own slaves (acquired souls) will keep mourning over him.” To contrast “fleshly relatives” and “acquired souls,” compare Ge 37:27 and Isa 58:7 with Ge (12:5; 14:21; 36:6); Eze 27:13; Re 18:13 ftn, “Souls.”"}]}],"13205":[{"footnoteId":4241,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1062,"text":"Lit., “knowledge of wind.” Heb., dha·ʽath-ruʹach."}]}],"13207":[{"footnoteId":4242,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1063,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]}],"13208":[{"footnoteId":4243,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1064,"text":"Or, “your mouth teaches your error.” LXX, “you are guilty by the words of your mouth”; Sy, “your mouth teaches sin.”"}]}],"13210":[{"footnoteId":4244,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1065,"text":"“Man.” Heb., ʼa·dhamʹ."}]}],"13211":[{"footnoteId":4245,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1066,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah."}]}],"13214":[{"footnoteId":4246,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1067,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]}],"13217":[{"footnoteId":4247,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1068,"text":"“Mortal man.” Heb., ʼenohshʹ."}]}],"13226":[{"footnoteId":4248,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1069,"text":"Or, “food.”"}]}],"13228":[{"footnoteId":4249,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1070,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]}],"13232":[{"footnoteId":4250,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1071,"text":"“Acquisition.” The meaning in M is uncertain; LXX, “shadow”; Vg, “root.”"}]}],"13233":[{"footnoteId":4251,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1072,"text":"“By a blast of.” Heb., beruʹach."}]}],"13235":[{"footnoteId":4252,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1073,"text":"Lit., “in not his day.”"}]}],"13241":[{"footnoteId":4253,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1074,"text":"Lit., “pains [offends].”"}]}],"13242":[{"footnoteId":4254,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1075,"text":"“Let me join words,” according to another derivation of the verb."}]}],"13249":[{"footnoteId":4255,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1076,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]},{"footnoteId":4256,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1077,"text":"Lit., “a young boy,” M; LXXVg, “an unjust one.”"}]}],"13254":[{"footnoteId":4257,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1078,"text":"Lit., “death shadow.”"}]}],"13257":[{"footnoteId":4258,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1079,"text":"“And my witness.” Heb., wesa·hadhiʹ, considered an Aram. loanword. See Ge 31:47 ftn, “Jegar-sahadutha.”"}]}],"13258":[{"footnoteId":4259,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1080,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah."}]}],"13259":[{"footnoteId":4260,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1081,"text":"“Man.” Heb., ʼa·dhamʹ."}]}],"13260":[{"footnoteId":4261,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1082,"text":"“Just numbered years,” LXX."}]}],"13261":[{"footnoteId":4262,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1083,"text":"Or, “breath.” See 12:10 ftn, “Spirit.”"}]}],"13276":[{"footnoteId":4263,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1084,"text":"“Sheol.” Heb., sheʼolʹ; Gr., haiʹden; Lat., in·ferʹnum. See App 4B."}]},{"footnoteId":4264,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1085,"text":"“They,” fem., referring to “hope,” twice in vs 15."}]}],"13283":[{"footnoteId":4265,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1086,"text":"Or, “uncanny power.”"}]}],"13289":[{"footnoteId":4266,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1087,"text":"“His skin will be eaten by disease,” by a slight correction of M."}]},{"footnoteId":4267,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1088,"text":"“The firstborn of death,” that is, the most deadly disease."}]}],"13294":[{"footnoteId":4268,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1089,"text":"“And from the productive land.” Heb., u·mit·te·velʹ; Lat., et de orʹbe, “and from the [terrestrial] circle.”"}]}],"13297":[{"footnoteId":4269,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1090,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]}],"13301":[{"footnoteId":4270,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1091,"text":"LXX adds: “by saying a thing that was not necessary, and my sayings (utterances) are mistaken (err) and not seasonable (timely).”"}]}],"13303":[{"footnoteId":4271,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1092,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah, sing. of ʼElo·himʹ."}]}],"13311":[{"footnoteId":4272,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1093,"text":"Or, “My relations.”"}]}],"13314":[{"footnoteId":4273,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1094,"text":"“My breath (spirit).” Heb., ru·chiʹ; Lat., haʹli·tum."}]}],"13317":[{"footnoteId":4274,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1095,"text":"“And my flesh becomes hairless in my teeth,” by another derivation of the verb and some corrections of M. Compare 13:14."}]}],"13318":[{"footnoteId":4275,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1096,"text":"“God’s.” Heb., ʼElohʹah."}]}],"13319":[{"footnoteId":4276,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1097,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]}],"13322":[{"footnoteId":4277,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1098,"text":"“My redeemer (repurchaser).” By extension of thought, “my avenger (vindicator).” Heb., goʹʼali; Lat., re·demʹptor. See Nu 35:21; Ps 19:14; Pr 23:11; Isa 63:16; Jer 50:34."}]}],"13323":[{"footnoteId":4278,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1099,"text":"Lit., “Yet out of my flesh,” or, “Yet apart from my flesh.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4279,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1100,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah."}]}],"13325":[{"footnoteId":4280,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1101,"text":"According to M; LXX, “we shall find in him.”"}]}],"13326":[{"footnoteId":4281,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1102,"text":"“There is a judge,” T and by a different vowel pointing of M (see 1Sa 24:15); others make it read, “there is an Almighty.”"}]}],"13330":[{"footnoteId":4282,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1103,"text":"Or, “Adam.” Heb., ʼa·dhamʹ."}]}],"13341":[{"footnoteId":4283,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1104,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]}],"13348":[{"footnoteId":4284,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1105,"text":"Lit., “hand.”"}]}],"13351":[{"footnoteId":4285,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1106,"text":"“Missile,” by a correction; M, “One has drawn out [a weapon].”"}]},{"footnoteId":4286,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1107,"text":"“A glittering weapon.” Lit., “lightning.”"}]}],"13354":[{"footnoteId":4287,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1108,"text":"Or, “The increase of his house will roll away.”"}]}],"13355":[{"footnoteId":4288,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1109,"text":"Or, “earthling man.” Heb., ʼa·dhamʹ."}]},{"footnoteId":4289,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1110,"text":"“From God.” Heb., me·ʼElo·himʹ."}]},{"footnoteId":4290,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1111,"text":"“From God.” Heb., me·ʼElʹ."}]}],"13364":[{"footnoteId":4291,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1112,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah. See 3:4 ftn."}]}],"13370":[{"footnoteId":4292,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1113,"text":"Or, “we should worship him (render him sacred service).” Heb., na·ʽav·dhenʹnu."}]}],"13371":[{"footnoteId":4293,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1114,"text":"Lit., “hand.”"}]}],"13373":[{"footnoteId":4294,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1115,"text":"“Wind.” Heb., ruʹach; Gr., a·neʹmou; Lat., venʹti."}]}],"13374":[{"footnoteId":4295,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1116,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah."}]}],"13377":[{"footnoteId":4296,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1117,"text":"“Even to God.” Heb., hal·ʼElʹ. See 22:2 ftn, “God.”"}]}],"13385":[{"footnoteId":4297,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1118,"text":"“He is delivered,” by a correction; M, “brought,” as in vs 32."}]}],"13387":[{"footnoteId":4298,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1119,"text":"Or, “heap of sheaves.”"}]}],"13388":[{"footnoteId":4299,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1120,"text":"Or, “every earthling man.” Heb., kol-ʼa·dhamʹ."}]}],"13391":[{"footnoteId":4300,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1121,"text":"“An able-bodied man.” Heb., gaʹver."}]},{"footnoteId":4301,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1122,"text":"“To God.” Heb., hal·ʼElʹ. Here ha is an interrogative particle introducing a question."}]}],"13397":[{"footnoteId":4302,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1123,"text":"“As for a man.” Heb., weʼishʹ."}]},{"footnoteId":4303,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1124,"text":"Lit., “arm.”"}]}],"13398":[{"footnoteId":4304,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1125,"text":"“Are crushed,” M; TLXXSyVg, “you crush.”"}]}],"13401":[{"footnoteId":4305,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1126,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah."}]},{"footnoteId":4306,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1127,"text":"“See,” M; LXXSy, “he sees.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4307,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1128,"text":"Or, “the head of the stars,” that is, the highest star."}]}],"13402":[{"footnoteId":4308,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1129,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]}],"13404":[{"footnoteId":4309,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1130,"text":"Lit., “men of hurtfulness.” Heb., metheh-ʼaʹwen."}]}],"13406":[{"footnoteId":4310,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1131,"text":"“To the [true] God.” Heb., la·ʼElʹ; LXX, “Jehovah.” See App 1G."}]},{"footnoteId":4311,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1132,"text":"“Against us,” LXXSy; M, “against him.”"}]}],"13409":[{"footnoteId":4312,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1133,"text":"“Our antagonists,” M; by a correction, “their property.”"}]}],"13415":[{"footnoteId":4313,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1134,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah."}]}],"13419":[{"footnoteId":4314,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1135,"text":"Possibly, “God will rescue the innocent one.” Lit., “He will rescue one not innocent.” M appears defective here."}]},{"footnoteId":4315,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1136,"text":"Lit., “palms.”"}]}],"13423":[{"footnoteId":4316,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1137,"text":"Or, “against.” Compare Ge 10:9 ftn, “Opposition to.”"}]}],"13426":[{"footnoteId":4317,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1138,"text":"Or, “from my opponent-at-law,” by a correction."}]}],"13428":[{"footnoteId":4318,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1139,"text":"“I turn aside,” SyVg."}]}],"13430":[{"footnoteId":4319,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1140,"text":"“Steps,” LXXSyVg; M, “step.”"}]}],"13435":[{"footnoteId":4320,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1141,"text":"“Even God.” Heb., weʼElʹ."}]}],"13438":[{"footnoteId":4321,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1142,"text":"“Together with its shepherd,” LXX."}]}],"13447":[{"footnoteId":4322,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1143,"text":"Or, “they press out oil.”"}]}],"13448":[{"footnoteId":4323,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1144,"text":"“And God.” Heb., we·ʼElohʹah."}]}],"13450":[{"footnoteId":4324,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1145,"text":"Or, “he goes as a burglar.”"}]}],"13458":[{"footnoteId":4325,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1146,"text":"“His life,” LXXVg and three Heb. mss; M, “life.”"}]}],"13465":[{"footnoteId":4326,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1147,"text":"“Mortal man.” Heb., ʼenohshʹ."}]},{"footnoteId":4327,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1148,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]}],"13467":[{"footnoteId":4328,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1149,"text":"Or, “earthling man.” Heb., ʼa·dhamʹ."}]}],"13471":[{"footnoteId":4329,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1150,"text":"“And whose breath.” Heb., wenish·math-miʹ."}]}],"13472":[{"footnoteId":4330,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1151,"text":"“Those impotent in death.” Heb., hor·pha·ʼimʹ; in earlier occurrences translated “the Rephaim”; LXXVg, “giants.”"}]}],"13473":[{"footnoteId":4331,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1152,"text":"“And [the place of] destruction.” Heb., la·ʼavad·dohnʹ, “Abaddon,” the first occurrence of this Heb. word; Gr., a·po·leiʹai; Lat., per·di·ti·oʹni. Compare “Apollyon” in Re 9:11 where see ftns."}]}],"13476":[{"footnoteId":4332,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1153,"text":"“The throne.” By a different vowel pointing, “his full moon.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4333,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1154,"text":"“Spreading out.” In Heb. the mixed form of this verb is understood to be in the infinitive absolute, indefinite as to time and impersonal."}]}],"13479":[{"footnoteId":4334,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1155,"text":"“The stormer.” Heb., raʹhav. Possibly a sea monster."}]}],"13480":[{"footnoteId":4335,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1156,"text":"“By his wind (spirit).” Heb., beru·chohʹ; Lat., spiʹri·tus."}]}],"13483":[{"footnoteId":4336,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1157,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]}],"13484":[{"footnoteId":4337,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1158,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah."}]}],"13489":[{"footnoteId":4338,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1159,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah."}]}],"13490":[{"footnoteId":4339,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1160,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]}],"13494":[{"footnoteId":4340,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1161,"text":"Or, “earthling man.” Heb., ʼa·dhamʹ."}]}],"13495":[{"footnoteId":4341,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1162,"text":"Or, “bread.”"}]}],"13496":[{"footnoteId":4342,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1163,"text":"Lit., “death.”"}]}],"13500":[{"footnoteId":4343,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1164,"text":"Or, “he will not be gathered,” M; LXXSy, “he will add nothing.”"}]}],"13501":[{"footnoteId":4344,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1165,"text":"“Like waters.” Or, “During the day,” by a correction."}]}],"13504":[{"footnoteId":4345,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1166,"text":"Or, “[one passing] his place will whistle at it.”"}]}],"13508":[{"footnoteId":4346,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1167,"text":"“Some of mortal men.” Heb., me·ʼenohshʹ."}]}],"13512":[{"footnoteId":4347,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1168,"text":"Lit., “The sons of pride (dignity).”"}]}],"13517":[{"footnoteId":4348,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1169,"text":"“Valuation,” MSyVg; LXX, “way.”"}]}],"13518":[{"footnoteId":4349,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1170,"text":"Or, “surging waters.” Heb., tehohmʹ, as in Ge 1:2; Gr., aʹbys·sos; Lat., a·bysʹsus."}]}],"13520":[{"footnoteId":4350,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1171,"text":"“With gold.” Heb., bekheʹthem, an Egyptian loanword."}]}],"13521":[{"footnoteId":4351,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1172,"text":"“Gold.” Heb., za·havʹ."}]}],"13523":[{"footnoteId":4352,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1173,"text":"“Cush,” M(Heb., Kush)Sy; LXXVg, “Ethiopia.”"}]}],"13526":[{"footnoteId":4353,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1174,"text":"“Destruction.” Heb., ʼavad·dohnʹ. See 26:6 ftn."}]}],"13527":[{"footnoteId":4354,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1175,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElo·himʹ."}]}],"13528":[{"footnoteId":4355,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1176,"text":"“Under the whole heavens,” MSy; LXXVg, “everything under the heavens.”"}]}],"13529":[{"footnoteId":4356,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1177,"text":"“For the wind.” Heb., la·ruʹach; Gr., a·neʹmon; Lat., venʹtis."}]}],"13531":[{"footnoteId":4357,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1178,"text":"Lit., “it,” fem., referring to wisdom."}]}],"13532":[{"footnoteId":4358,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1179,"text":"Or, “to earthling man.” Heb., la·ʼa·dhamʹ."}]},{"footnoteId":4359,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1180,"text":"One of 134 scribal changes from YHWH to ʼAdho·naiʹ. See App 1B."}]}],"13534":[{"footnoteId":4360,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1181,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah."}]}],"13538":[{"footnoteId":4361,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1182,"text":"Lit., “was being poured out as streams of oil with me.”"}]}],"13549":[{"footnoteId":4362,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1183,"text":"“Tear,” by a slight correction; M, “throw.”"}]}],"13550":[{"footnoteId":4363,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1184,"text":"“Within my nest.” Possibly, “In my old age,” to agree with LXX."}]}],"13572":[{"footnoteId":4364,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1185,"text":"“Like the wind.” Heb., ka·ruʹach. See Ge 1:2 ftn, “Force.”"}]}],"13585":[{"footnoteId":4365,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1186,"text":"“Sunlight,” M; by a correction, “comfort.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4366,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1187,"text":"“In the congregation.” Heb., vaq·qa·halʹ; Gr., ek·kle·siʹai."}]}],"13590":[{"footnoteId":4367,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1188,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah; Gr., ho The·osʹ."}]}],"13594":[{"footnoteId":4368,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1189,"text":"Lit., “in scales of righteousness.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4369,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1190,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah; LXX, “Jehovah.”"}]}],"13600":[{"footnoteId":4370,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1191,"text":"“Destruction.” Heb., ʼavad·dohnʹ. See 26:6 ftn."}]}],"13602":[{"footnoteId":4371,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1192,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]}],"13611":[{"footnoteId":4372,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1193,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl; Gr., Ky·riʹou, “Jehovah.”"}]}],"13612":[{"footnoteId":4373,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1194,"text":"“Gold.” Heb., za·havʹ."}]},{"footnoteId":4374,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1195,"text":"“Or to gold.” Heb., welak·keʹthem. See 28:16 ftn."}]}],"13615":[{"footnoteId":4375,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1196,"text":"Apparently alluding to throwing a kiss with the hand in an idolatrous practice. Kissing of idols is mentioned in 1Ki 19:18; Ho 13:2."}]}],"13617":[{"footnoteId":4376,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1197,"text":"“Felt excited,” M; T, “made a joyful noise.”"}]}],"13619":[{"footnoteId":4377,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1198,"text":"Lit., “flesh; meat.”"}]}],"13620":[{"footnoteId":4378,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1199,"text":"“Path,” M; TLXXSyVg, “traveler.”"}]}],"13621":[{"footnoteId":4379,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1200,"text":"“Like an earthling man (Adam; man).” Heb., kheʼa·dhamʹ, possibly, “from man; among men.”"}]}],"13623":[{"footnoteId":4380,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1201,"text":"Lit., “mark,” evidently in writing, confirming a legal document."}]},{"footnoteId":4381,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1202,"text":"Lit., “man.” Heb., ʼish."}]}],"13627":[{"footnoteId":4382,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1203,"text":"Lit., “its power.” Heb., ko·chahʹ."}]}],"13629":[{"footnoteId":4383,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1204,"text":"“His,” M; LXXSy, “their.”"}]}],"13630":[{"footnoteId":4384,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1205,"text":"Meaning “My God Is He.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4385,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1206,"text":"“Than God.” Heb., me·ʼElo·himʹ; LXX, “Jehovah.”"}]}],"13631":[{"footnoteId":4386,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1207,"text":"“God,” originally. M, “Job.” The Jewish Sopherim changed the original text from “God” to “Job.” This is one of the Eighteen Emendations. See App 2B."}]}],"13634":[{"footnoteId":4387,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1208,"text":"Or, “I feared.” Heb., za·chalʹti."}]}],"13641":[{"footnoteId":4388,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1209,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]}],"13649":[{"footnoteId":4389,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1210,"text":"“Man.” Heb., ʼish."}]},{"footnoteId":4390,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1211,"text":"“Earthling man.” Heb., ʼa·dhamʹ."}]}],"13651":[{"footnoteId":4391,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1212,"text":"“My words.” Heb., mil·laiʹ."}]},{"footnoteId":4392,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1213,"text":"Lit., “my words.” Heb., deva·raiʹ."}]}],"13654":[{"footnoteId":4393,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1214,"text":"Lit., “The spirit of God.” Heb., ru·ach-ʼElʹ."}]}],"13662":[{"footnoteId":4394,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1215,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah."}]}],"13664":[{"footnoteId":4395,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1216,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]}],"13667":[{"footnoteId":4396,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1217,"text":"Or, “an earthling man.” Heb., ʼa·dhamʹ."}]},{"footnoteId":4397,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1218,"text":"“From an able-bodied man.” Heb., mig·geʹver."}]}],"13668":[{"footnoteId":4398,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1219,"text":"“From passing away by a missile.” BHK proposes corrections that would make this read, “from passing over into Sheol,” thus running parallel with “pit” in the first part of the vs."}]}],"13672":[{"footnoteId":4399,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1220,"text":"“To those inflicting death.” By a correction of M, “to dead ones”; or, “to the place of dead ones.”"}]}],"13673":[{"footnoteId":4400,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1221,"text":"Or, “an angel.” Lat., anʹge·lus."}]},{"footnoteId":4401,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1222,"text":"Or, “an interpreter.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4402,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1223,"text":"“His uprightness,” M; LXX, “his own blame. He will show his want of understanding.”"}]}],"13674":[{"footnoteId":4403,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1224,"text":"Or, “covering.” Heb., khoʹpher."}]}],"13676":[{"footnoteId":4404,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1225,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah; LXX, “Jehovah.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4405,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1226,"text":"“To mortal man.” Heb., le·ʼenohshʹ."}]}],"13678":[{"footnoteId":4406,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1227,"text":"“My,” MLXXSy; MmarginTVg, “his.”"}]}],"13679":[{"footnoteId":4407,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1228,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]}],"13680":[{"footnoteId":4408,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1229,"text":"According to M; Sy, “to see the light.”"}]}],"13688":[{"footnoteId":4409,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1230,"text":"“But God.” Heb., weʼElʹ."}]}],"13690":[{"footnoteId":4410,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1231,"text":"“Able-bodied man.” Heb., gheʹver."}]}],"13692":[{"footnoteId":4411,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1232,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElo·himʹ; LXX, “Jehovah.”"}]}],"13693":[{"footnoteId":4412,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1233,"text":"“From the [true] God.” Heb., la·ʼElʹ; LXX, “Jehovah.” See App 1G."}]}],"13694":[{"footnoteId":4413,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1234,"text":"“Earthling man.” Heb., ʼa·dhamʹ."}]},{"footnoteId":4414,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1235,"text":"“Man.” Heb., ʼish."}]}],"13695":[{"footnoteId":4415,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1236,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl; LXX, “Jehovah.”"}]}],"13696":[{"footnoteId":4416,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1237,"text":"“Productive land.” Heb., te·velʹ; Lat., orʹbem, “circle,” that is, of the earth."}]}],"13698":[{"footnoteId":4417,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1238,"text":"“And earthling man.” Heb., weʼa·dhamʹ."}]}],"13701":[{"footnoteId":4418,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1239,"text":"Lit., “Shall there be a saying.” In Heb. this is a verb in the infinitive construct, indefinite as to time and impersonal."}]},{"footnoteId":4419,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1240,"text":"Lit., “king, ‘Belial!’?”"}]}],"13704":[{"footnoteId":4420,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1241,"text":"Or, “each one.” Heb., ʼish, as in vs 23."}]}],"13706":[{"footnoteId":4421,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1242,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]}],"13712":[{"footnoteId":4422,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1243,"text":"Or, “an earthling man.” Heb., ʼa·dhamʹ."}]}],"13719":[{"footnoteId":4423,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1244,"text":"Or, “O that Job may be tested.”"}]}],"13720":[{"footnoteId":4424,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1245,"text":"“Against the [true] God.” Heb., la·ʼElʹ. See App 1G."}]}],"13722":[{"footnoteId":4425,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1246,"text":"“More than God’s.” Heb., me·ʼElʹ; LXX, “Jehovah.”"}]}],"13724":[{"footnoteId":4426,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1247,"text":"“Companions,” M; LXX, “three friends.”"}]}],"13728":[{"footnoteId":4427,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1248,"text":"“Against a man.” Heb., leʼishʹ."}]},{"footnoteId":4428,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1249,"text":"“Earthling man.” Heb., ʼa·dhamʹ."}]}],"13730":[{"footnoteId":4429,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1250,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah."}]},{"footnoteId":4430,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1251,"text":"“Grand Maker,” pl. in M, to denote excellence and grandeur, although “God” is sing."}]}],"13731":[{"footnoteId":4431,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1252,"text":"Or, “the domestic animals.”"}]}],"13733":[{"footnoteId":4432,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1253,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]}],"13738":[{"footnoteId":4433,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1254,"text":"“For God.” Heb., le·ʼElohʹah."}]}],"13739":[{"footnoteId":4434,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1255,"text":"Or, “and to my Maker.” Heb., u·lePho·ʽaliʹ."}]}],"13741":[{"footnoteId":4435,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1256,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]},{"footnoteId":4436,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1257,"text":"Or, “good motive.” Compare 34:34."}]}],"13756":[{"footnoteId":4437,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1258,"text":"Or, “night’s [rest].”"}]}],"13758":[{"footnoteId":4438,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1259,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]}],"13761":[{"footnoteId":4439,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1260,"text":"“Mankind.” Heb., ʼa·dhamʹ."}]}],"13768":[{"footnoteId":4440,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1261,"text":"Lit., “light.” Heb., ʼohr, the same noun as in vs 30."}]}],"13772":[{"footnoteId":4441,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1262,"text":"Lit., “wings.”"}]}],"13774":[{"footnoteId":4442,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1263,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]}],"13779":[{"footnoteId":4443,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1264,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]},{"footnoteId":4444,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1265,"text":"Or, “is frozen.”"}]}],"13781":[{"footnoteId":4445,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1266,"text":"“Productive land of,” M(Heb., the·velʹ)T; Lat., orʹbis, “circle,” that is, of the earth."}]}],"13782":[{"footnoteId":4446,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1267,"text":"Symbolizing correction or chastisement."}]},{"footnoteId":4447,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1268,"text":"Or, “loyal love.”"}]}],"13784":[{"footnoteId":4448,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1269,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah."}]}],"13786":[{"footnoteId":4449,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1270,"text":"Or, “when there is a quieting of the earth.”"}]}],"13790":[{"footnoteId":4450,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1271,"text":"“When a wind.” Heb., weruʹach. See Ge 1:2 ftn, “Force.”"}]}],"13791":[{"footnoteId":4451,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1272,"text":"Lit., “gold.” Heb., za·havʹ."}]},{"footnoteId":4452,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1273,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah."}]}],"13793":[{"footnoteId":4453,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1274,"text":"“Men.” Heb., ʼana·shimʹ, pl. of ʼish."}]}],"13800":[{"footnoteId":4454,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1275,"text":"“Sons of God.” Or, “godlike ones.” Heb., benehʹ ʼElo·himʹ; T, “the bands of angels”; LXX, “my angels.”"}]}],"13801":[{"footnoteId":4455,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1276,"text":"Or, “double doors,” as in 2Ch 14:7."}]}],"13802":[{"footnoteId":4456,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1277,"text":"That is, the sea’s."}]}],"13803":[{"footnoteId":4457,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1278,"text":"“Break up,” M; LXX, “put.”"}]}],"13806":[{"footnoteId":4458,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1279,"text":"Lit., “wings.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4459,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1280,"text":"“The wicked ones.” Here in M the Heb. letter ʽAʹyin (ע) is suspended as an insertion to indicate that the word should read “wicked ones” instead of “poor ones.” Compare Jg 18:30 ftn, “Moses’.”"}]}],"13807":[{"footnoteId":4460,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1281,"text":"Lit., “they.”"}]}],"13808":[{"footnoteId":4461,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1282,"text":"See vs 13 ftn, “Ones.”"}]}],"13809":[{"footnoteId":4462,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1283,"text":"Or, “sandy ground.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4463,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1284,"text":"Or, “surging waters.” See 28:14 ftn."}]}],"13810":[{"footnoteId":4464,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1285,"text":"Lit., “death shadow,” M; LXX, “Hades,” that is, the common grave; T, “death of Gehenna.”"}]}],"13817":[{"footnoteId":4465,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1286,"text":"“Hoarfrost,” LXX."}]}],"13819":[{"footnoteId":4466,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1287,"text":"“Man.” Heb., ʼish."}]},{"footnoteId":4467,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1288,"text":"“Earthling man.” Heb., ʼa·dhamʹ. See Ge 1:26 ftn, “Man.”"}]}],"13824":[{"footnoteId":4468,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1289,"text":"See 9:9 ftn, “Kimah constellation.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4469,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1290,"text":"See 9:9 ftn, “Kesil constellation.”"}]}],"13825":[{"footnoteId":4470,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1291,"text":"“The Mazzaroth constellation.” Heb., Maz·za·rohthʹ; Gr., Ma·zou·rothʹ (as in 2Ki 23:5 where it is translated “constellations of the zodiac”); Sy, “the Wagon constellation”; Lat., lu·ciʹfe·rum, “the light bearer.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4471,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1292,"text":"See 9:9 ftn, “Ash constellation.”"}]}],"13829":[{"footnoteId":4472,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1293,"text":"“In the cloud layers.” Heb., bat·tu·chohthʹ, the meaning is uncertain."}]},{"footnoteId":4473,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1294,"text":"“To the sky phenomenon.” Heb., las·sekhʹwi, the meaning is uncertain but appears to refer to some heavenly phenomenon."}]}],"13832":[{"footnoteId":4474,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1295,"text":"Lit., “fill.”"}]}],"13834":[{"footnoteId":4475,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1296,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]}],"13837":[{"footnoteId":4476,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1297,"text":"Or, “let loose their fetuses.”"}]}],"13851":[{"footnoteId":4477,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1298,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah."}]}],"13853":[{"footnoteId":4478,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1299,"text":"“A rustling mane,” M; T, “strength.”"}]}],"13855":[{"footnoteId":4479,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1300,"text":"“It paws,” LXXSyVg; M, “They paw.”"}]}],"13859":[{"footnoteId":4480,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1301,"text":"Lit., “princes.” Heb., sa·rimʹ."}]}],"13866":[{"footnoteId":4481,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1302,"text":"“Should there be any contending.” In Heb. this is a verb in the infinitive absolute, indefinite as to time and impersonal."}]},{"footnoteId":4482,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1303,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼElohʹah."}]}],"13872":[{"footnoteId":4483,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1304,"text":"“Do you imagine that I have treated you otherwise than that you should appear righteous?” LXX."}]}],"13873":[{"footnoteId":4484,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1305,"text":"“Like that of the [true] God.” Heb., ka·ʼElʹ. See De 33:26 ftn, “God.”"}]}],"13879":[{"footnoteId":4485,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1306,"text":"Or, “hippopotamus.” Heb., vehe·mohthʹ, pl. of behe·mahʹ (compare Ge 1:24 ftn, “Animal”); Gr., the·riʹa; Lat.(vs 10), Be·heʹmoth."}]}],"13883":[{"footnoteId":4486,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1307,"text":"“God.” Heb., ʼEl."}]}],"13884":[{"footnoteId":4487,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1308,"text":"“He made pleasure for the four-footed creatures in the Tartarus,” LXX. See App 4D."}]}],"13888":[{"footnoteId":4488,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1309,"text":"MLXX continue this chapter for eight more vss."}]}],"13889":[{"footnoteId":4489,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1310,"text":"“Leviathan,” M(Heb., liw·ya·thanʹ)Vg; LXX, “a dragon.”"}]}],"13894":[{"footnoteId":4490,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1311,"text":"Or, “make a feast over it.”"}]},{"footnoteId":4491,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1312,"text":"Lit., “Canaanites.” Heb., kena·ʽanimʹ."}]}],"13896":[{"footnoteId":4492,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1313,"text":"MLXX end chapter 40 here."}]}],"13901":[{"footnoteId":4493,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1314,"text":"Lit., “bridle,” M; LXX, “scale armor [coat of mail].”"}]}],"13902":[{"footnoteId":4494,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1315,"text":"“Face,” M; Sy, “mouth.”"}]}],"13905":[{"footnoteId":4495,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1316,"text":"Lit., “to its brother.”"}]}],"13909":[{"footnoteId":4496,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1317,"text":"“Its soul.” Heb., naph·shohʹ; Gr., psy·kheʹ."}]}],"13910":[{"footnoteId":4497,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1318,"text":"“Despair leaps,” M; LXX, “destruction runs.”"}]}],"13916":[{"footnoteId":4498,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1319,"text":"Lit., “A son of a bow.”"}]}],"13918":[{"footnoteId":4499,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1320,"text":"Or, “The most pointed (sharpest) of earthenware fragments,” according to the Heb. idiom."}]}],"13920":[{"footnoteId":4500,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1321,"text":"“And the Tartarus of the abyss as a captive,” LXX. See App 4D."}]},{"footnoteId":4501,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1322,"text":"“As gray-headedness,” M; LXX, “as a place to walk”; Sy, “as the dry land.”"}]}],"13922":[{"footnoteId":4502,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1323,"text":"Lit., “all the sons of pride (dignity).”"}]}],"13927":[{"footnoteId":4503,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1324,"text":"Or, “In a report to the ear.”"}]}],"13928":[{"footnoteId":4504,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1325,"text":"Or, “I do feel regret.”"}]}],"13933":[{"footnoteId":4505,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1326,"text":"Lit., “give him one qesitah.” A money unit of unknown value."}]}],"13934":[{"footnoteId":4506,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1327,"text":"See 1:3 ftn, “Sheep.”"}]}],"13938":[{"footnoteId":4507,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1328,"text":"“But Job lived after the plague a hundred and seventy years; all the [years] that he lived were two hundred and forty-eight [LXXא,B omit “eight”] years,” LXX."}]}],"13939":[{"footnoteId":4508,"paragraphs":[{"pid":1329,"text":"LXX adds: “And it has been written that he will rise again with those whom Jehovah raises up. This [man] is described from the Syriac book as residing in the land of Ausitis [Uz], on the borders of Idumea and Arabia. And formerly his name was Jobab. After taking an Arabian wife, he became father to a son whose name was Ennon. But he himself was the son of his father Zare, a son of the sons of Esau, but [was the son] of his mother Bosorrha, so that he was the fifth [in line] from Abraham. And these are the kings that reigned in Edom, of which country he also was ruler: first, Balak, the son of Beor, and the name of his city was Dennaba; but after Balak, Jobab, the one called Job; but after this one Asom, who happened to be governor out of the country of Thaimanitis; but after this one Adad, the son of Barad, who cut off Madiam in the plain of Moab, and the name of his city was Gethaim. But the friends that came to him [were] Eliphaz, of the sons of Esau, king of the Thaimanites; Bildad the absolute ruler of the Sauchaians; Zophar the king of the Minaians.”"}]}]}